 "method": "Each lateral frame cropped from the full scan at 1-2.5x with a grid labelled in scan pixels (contrast raised), plus brightness-run profiles across the legs. A foot is 'down' when heel, sole or toe rests on the walkway board; a foot whose sole is within a few pixels of the board and could be either landing or lifting is left out. Legs are tracked by continuity from frame to frame. Only what could be identified with confidence is recorded. Near leg/arm = the sunlit side nearest the camera (the leading leg in frame 1); far leg = the other. Joint points (hip, knee, ankle, toe, heel; shoulder, elbow, wrist of the near arm) were placed on the 2x crops, drawn back onto the crops as dots and lines, checked by eye and corrected (frames 5-6 near knee moved 6 px; frame 7 near toe/heel dropped). The hip point is the estimated hip-joint centre at the level of the pubis, mid-depth of the pelvis (one point used for both legs); it carries about +/-8 px of uncertainty, i.e. +/-4-6 deg on thigh angles. Angles by atan2 from verified points only: thigh/upperArm = segment direction from straight down, + = forward (direction of travel); knee = thigh minus shank angle (flexion +); ankle = inner angle knee-ankle-toe (90 = foot square to shank); elbowFlex = forearm minus upper arm direction.",
